<title>USA: Hibbett Sporting Q1 shr $0.23 vs $0.24.</title>
<headline>Hibbett Sporting Q1 shr $0.23 vs $0.24.</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, Ala. 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>HIBBETT SPORTING GOODS, INC.</p>
<p>		  Unaudited Statements of Operations</p>
<p>	     (In thousands, except earnings per share data)</p>
<p>						     First Quarter Ended</p>
<p>							 May 3,	May 4,</p>
<p>							   1997     1996(a)</p>
<p>						     (13 weeks)(13 weeks)</p>
<p> Net Sales					   $26,165    $20,251</p>
<p>Cost of goods sold, including warehouse,</p>
<p>   distribution, and store occupancy costs  18,126     14,035</p>
<p>   Gross profit					8,039	6,216</p>
<p>Store operating, selling and  administrative</p>
<p>   expenses					    5,241	3,394</p>
<p> Depreciation and amortization		     517	  393</p>
<p>   Operating income				  2,281	2,429</p>
<p> Interest expense (income), net		   (25)	  910</p>
<p>   Income before provision for income taxes  2,306	1,519</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes			  882	  584</p>
<p>   Net income					  1,424	  935</p>
<p>Earnings per common share:</p>
<p>   Net income					   0.23	 0.24</p>
<p> Weighted average shares outstanding	   6,235	3,896</p>
<p>NOTES: Store operating, selling and administrative expenses for the 13-week period ended May 4, 1996, include a one-time gain of $513,000 on the sale of the company's former headquarters and distribution center.</p>
<p>Excluding this one-time gain, store operating, selling and administrative expenses would have been $3.9 million, operating income would have been $1.9 million, and net income would have been $619,000 or $.16 per share.</p>
</text>
